# Components: the shared spec ({{PLATFORMS}})

One spec per component, the same on every platform. Token names are paths in
`assets/tokens/{{SLUG}}.tokens.json` ({{TOK_EXAMPLES}} ...). How each one
is built per platform is in the platform files linked from [SKILL.md](../SKILL.md). Where each exists today:
[inventory.md](inventory.md).

**Every component, every platform:** states default, pressed or active, focused (keyboard ring on web, accessibility focus
on mobile), disabled (still readable), loading where it acts, error where it takes input, selected where it can be chosen.
Touch targets at least 44pt (iOS), 48dp (Android) or 44px on touch web layouts, even when the drawing is smaller. Motion per
[motion.md](motion.md); accessibility per [accessibility.md](accessibility.md). This list is the starting set: edit it as the
product's real components are decided, and keep [inventory.md](inventory.md) in step.

## Primitives

### Button
| | |
|---|---|
| Purpose | Start an action. Exactly one primary per view. |
| Anatomy | Optional leading icon, label (verb + object, see [vocabulary.md](vocabulary.md)), spinner while loading. |
| Variants | primary (`primary` / `on-primary`), secondary (`surface`, 1px `outline-input`), ghost (no chrome), link (`link`), destructive (`danger` / `on-danger`, confirmations only). |
| Sizes | sm, md, lg; icon-only is square. Radius {{TOK_RADIUS_CONTROL}}. Text {{TOK_TYPE_LABEL}}. |
| States | loading: spinner, activation blocked, focus kept. Disabled: reduced opacity, still readable. |
| A11y | The visible text is the label; icon-only buttons need an accessible label (and a tooltip on web). |

### Input (text field)
| | |
|---|---|
| Purpose | One line of text, a number or a date. |
| Anatomy | Label above, field, helper or error text under it. |
| Tokens | `surface`, border `outline-input`, focus border `primary` plus the focus ring, invalid border `danger`. |
| States | focus, invalid (border and words, announced), disabled, read-only. |
| A11y | Label tied to the field; error linked to it. Never show an error on the first keystroke. |

### Select, checkbox, radio, switch
| | |
|---|---|
| Purpose | Choose one or several from a known list; switch is for an immediate on/off. |
| Rules | Use the platform's accessible primitive. A switch applies at once; a checkbox waits for submit. |
| States | unchecked, checked, indeterminate (checkbox), focus, disabled, invalid. |
| A11y | The label is clickable and 44px tall; groups have a legend. |

### Card
| | |
|---|---|
| Purpose | Group related content on `surface`. |
| Tokens | `surface`, 1px `outline`, {{TOK_RADIUS_CARD}}, {{TOK_SHADOW_CARD}} only when it lifts above the page. |
| Rules | A card that is clickable is one control with one focus ring; never nest clickable cards. |

### Badge and chip
| | |
|---|---|
| Purpose | A short status or category. Status is always a word plus an icon. |
| Tokens | Neutral on `sunk`; status uses the `success` / `danger` pairs. |

### Dialog and sheet
| | |
|---|---|
| Purpose | Dialog: a decision that blocks. Sheet: a task on the side (web) or bottom (mobile). |
| Rules | Focus moves in and is trapped; Escape or back closes; focus returns to the trigger. One primary action. |
| A11y | Title is the accessible name; the scrim is `scrim` and never the only boundary. |

### Menu, tabs, tooltip
Use the platform primitives. Menus open on the keyboard, arrows move, Escape closes. Tabs show the selected one with more
than colour. Tooltips never hold information that is not available elsewhere.

### Toast
| | |
|---|---|
| Purpose | Confirm something that already happened. |
| Rules | Announced politely; stays at least 5 seconds; never the only way to learn about an error; offers undo for reversible actions. |

## Patterns

### Empty state
An icon, one line saying what is missing and why, one action that fixes it. Never a blank area.

### Error state
What happened in words, what to do next, a retry. Keep the user's input. Never only red.

### Skeleton
Same layout as the content, shown after 200 ms, no flashing; the only continuous animation besides the in-button spinner.

### Page header
Title ({{TOK_TYPE_TITLE}}), optional description, primary action at the end. One per page.

### App shell
Navigation, page area, optional side panel. Navigation model and responsive behaviour are in [ux.md](ux.md).
